- stage_schedule_candidate (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading). Wait stage_schedule_candidate precondition includes not origin_leg_loaded? Actually stage_schedule_candidate has precondition: (candidate_prepared ?candidate) (candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container) (loading_container_loaded ?loading_container) (loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile) (not (origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg)) (not (candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate)). So we need origin_leg_loaded false. Since we haven't loaded origin leg (we only loaded container onto leg, not origin leg loaded). The origin_leg_loaded predicate is set by assemble_origin_loaded_leg etc. We haven't done those. So origin_leg_loaded false, good.

- verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_loading_verified). We'll have destination_leg_loaded false.

- establish_clearance_nominal (requires candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established). Good.

- finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized). Since we haven't set route_sequence_context_set (we didn't do any of the establish_clearance_* that set route_sequence_context_set? Actually establish_clearance_nominal does NOT set route_sequence_context_set (only the other establish_clearance actions do). So route_sequence_context_set remains false. Good.

- Then allocate dispatch slot and execute schedule dispatch.

Thus we need to do for each schedule candidate: load its container, stage, verify loading, establish clearance, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch.

Now we need to ensure we have enough loading containers: we have loading_container_alpha and loading_container_beta. Each schedule candidate has one linked: shift_candidate_alpha linked to loading_container_alpha, shift_candidate_beta to loading_container_beta. Good.

Now we need to assign operator, skill cert, compliance cert to each schedule candidate. We have only one operator resource (driver_operator_alpha), one skill certificate (skill_certificate_alpha), one compliance certificate (compliance_certificate_alpha). However each schedule candidate needs its own links; but after we assign to one candidate, the resource becomes unavailable (not available). We could release after use? There are release actions: release_operator_resource, release_skill_certificate, release_compliance_certificate. So we can assign to first candidate, then after we finish with that candidate (maybe after finalize/dispatch), we can release and assign to second. However the schedule candidate needs operator linked etc at the time of verification and clearance establishment. After establishing clearance, we could release them? The predicates candidate_operator_linked etc are used in later steps? For finalize_candidate_direct we only need candidate_clearance_established, not operator etc. So we could release after establishing clearance, before finalizing? Actually finalize_candidate_direct does not require operator/link. So we could release after establishing clearance but before finalize? However we need candidate_clearance_established to stay true; releasing operator does not affect that. So we can release after establishing clearance.

